  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At the heart of the Estéron gorges, the Clue de Saint-Auban reveals a wide pool with jade-green reflections, framed by steep rock walls and the ruins of an old mill that recall the site's industrial past.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to Randoxygène (Alpes-Maritimes department), the scenic road overlooking the clue lets you see all of it, and access to the Estéron riverbed is on foot in about 5 minutes from the entrance of the clue, via the road and then sloping slabs. The site mainly attracts canyoners: the descent is only possible at low water, from 1 April to 31 October, on Mondays, Wednesdays, Fridays and Sundays from 9am to 5pm — a sign of the risks tied to the Estéron's flow. No specific information on dogs was found for this site: apply a leash by default, as everywhere out in nature in the department.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: stay alert to any unusual movement of water in the pools, even during an ordinary swim — flash floods on the Estéron can rise very quickly after a storm upstream, sometimes without any visible rain on site.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Clue d'Aiglun, a little further south in the same Estéron valley, is another Estéron site, mostly visited by canyoners (see the dedicated listing).</p>
    </div>

